  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{暗|あん} (dark, implicit) + {示|じ} (show, indicate) - showing implicitly\n\nUSAGE:\nCan describe:\n- Hidden meanings in words or actions\n- Foreshadowing in stories\n- Psychological suggestion\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {自己暗示|じこあんじ} - self-suggestion, autosuggestion\n- {暗示|あんじ}にかかる - to be susceptible to suggestion\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {暗示|あんじ}を{与|あた}える - to give a hint\n- {暗示|あんじ}に{富|と}む - to be full of suggestions/implications\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {含|ふく}み - implication, undertone\n- {婉曲|えんきょく} - euphemism\n- ほのめかす - to hint, suggest",
